======================================================================
WEEK 6 FINALE: OpenAI fine-tuning  (NOT run in this offline project)
======================================================================

The real course finishes Week 6 by FINE-TUNING a frontier model:
  1. Convert training items into a JSONL file of chat examples.
  2. Upload it and launch a PAID OpenAI fine-tuning job
     (client.fine_tuning.jobs.create on gpt-4o-mini).
  3. Monitor the job with Weights & Biases (W&B) integration.
  4. Evaluate the fine-tuned model vs. the ML baselines.

We do NOT run this here because it requires:
  - a paid OpenAI API key (fine-tuning is not free),
  - the large real Amazon dataset for meaningful training,
  - a W&B account for tracking.

Shape of ONE JSONL training row (one line per example in the file):
----------------------------------------------------------------------
{
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "You estimate prices of items. Reply only with the price, no explanation."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "How much does this cost?\n\nStark pro laptop in excellent condition, barely used."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Price is $1623.40"
    }
  ]
}
----------------------------------------------------------------------

As a single JSONL line it would look like:
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You estimate prices of items. Reply only with the price, no explanation."}, {"role": "user", "content": "How much does this cost?\n\nStark pro laptop in excellent condition, barely used."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Price is $1623.40"}]}

To actually run it you would then do roughly:
  openai.files.create(file=open('train.jsonl','rb'), purpose='fine-tune')
  openai.fine_tuning.jobs.create(training_file=<id>, model='gpt-4o-mini')
